  {
   "name": "loop-invokes-an-action-per-iteration",
   "_note_idiom": "for…of is THE portable loop idiom (green on all three runtimes). A classic `for (let i=0; i<n; i++)` is NON-PORTABLE: in a native action `x=e` always writes the STORE, so the `let i` local shadows the read and the loop spins to the budget on iOS+Android (pinned bug-for-bug, JseRunner.kt NOTES). Authors use for…of or a store-var counter `for (i=0; …)`; a lint rule flags classic-for-with-let (W7).",
   "actions": {
    "fill": {
     "body": "for (const n of [0, 1, 2]) { dsx.action.pushOne({ v: n }) }"
    },
    "pushOne": {
     "body": "dsx.variable.items.push(v)"
    }
   },
   "scope": {
    "items": []
   },
   "run": "fill",
   "expectStore": {
    "items": [
     0,
     1,
     2
    ]
   },
   "expectEvents": []
  },
